


#Backend

To get the server running
# NPM INSTALL
1. cd Backend
2. npm run dev
3. it will get your port running on localhost:5000
4. it is a static object database, so creating account doesn't mean it will be stored in a real database.
5. i purposely removed the .env from .gitignore for faster testing since this is not real world application, just for learning.
6. Testing the Endpoint /5000/register/JSON{
"username": "ishaka007" , "email": "ishakaprecious735@gmail.com", "password": " 03938u3uywuy"
}

7. Login  /5000/login/JSON{
 "email": "ishakaprecious735@gmail.com", "password": " 03938u3uywuy"
}


#Frontend
# NPM INSTALL and Install Angular 21 globally
1. cd frontend
2. ng s (To get the Angular frontend server running)
